Now the smoke test expects portrait at 390x844 -> 2.16 yes. landscape 844x390 -> 0.46 yes. Good.

But CSS still uses media (max-width:800) for dock layout. At 740x360, max-width 800 applies and grid areas 2 rows, dock height 127, leaving only 233 of board; but with landscape scale 0.45 board 576x360, pads at y648*.45=292-20=272; dock top 360-6-127=227 -> pads hidden under dock. Ugh. The max-width 800 dock layout (two rows) is used for narrow landscape phones, making dock tall. Need to adjust CSS for short landscape regardless of width. The `@media (max-height: 620px) and (orientation: landscape)` block comes after max-width:800 and should override some sizes, but not grid areas. It sets cards 44, power 44, wave 44, but the max-width:800 grid-template-areas remains "build build"/"powers wave", so dock height = 44+44+gap+padding ~100. Still tall.

We should unify: for short landscape, use single-row dock even if width <=800. In the max-height block, set:
```
.dock {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) 1px auto auto;
  grid-template-areas: none;
  width: calc(100vw - 12px);
  gap: 8px;
}
.build-group { grid-area: auto; }
.power-group { grid-area: auto; justify-content: flex-end; }
.dock-sep { display: block; height: 44px; margin-bottom: 0; }
```
But max-width:800 media sets `.dock-sep { display:none }`. Override display:block in short landscape. However the dock content width at 740: build group 4*94 + 12 gaps = 388; sep 1; powers 2*44+4=92; wave 118; gaps 3*8=24; padding 16 => 639, fits in 728. Good. At 667x375, width 655: 388+1+92+118+24+16=639 fits. At 568x320, width 556: 639 doesn't fit; grid minmax may shrink build group but tower cards fixed 94 => overflow. Need smaller cards for <=700 width short landscape. Could set tower-card width 70 or use 4 columns grid? Hmm.

Devices with landscape width <640 are rare (iPhone SE landscape 667). 568x320 is very old iPhone 5, not important. But we should avoid overflow. Set `.dock { width: calc(100vw - 12px); }`; tower cards width 80? At 568: 4*80+12=332 +1+92+118+24+16=583 >556. Could reduce wave to 100, powers 40, cards 75 =>328... still. Maybe hide the dock-sep and reduce gaps. 328+88+100+16+16=548 fits. For 667, great. So in short landscape:
- `.dock { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) auto auto; grid-template-areas: none; width: calc(100vw - 12px); gap: 7px; padding:4px 7px; }`
- `.dock-sep { display:none; }` (build, powers, wave)
- `.build-group { grid-area:auto; } .power-group { grid-area:auto; }`
- `.tower-list { display:flex; gap:3px; }`
- `.tower-card { width: 78px; height:44px; }` (base 94 overridden; max-width 800 sets width:auto for grid, but then `display:flex` and width auto would size to content; set width 78)
- On wider landscape 844, cards 78 -> 4*78+9=321; leaves more space. Fine. Could set width 82.
- `.tower-icon { 27 }`.
- Powers 44, wave 110.

At 740: 4*82+9=337 + 88 + 110 + gaps 3*7=21 + padding 14 = 570 <728. Plenty.
At 568: 337+88+110+21+14=570 >556 by 14. Could shrink card to 78 -> 321 total 554 fits. Use 78.
At 480x320 landscape (very small): 480-12=468, still too much. Could hide power buttons or allow scroll? Not critical, 480x320 is rare. But maybe iPhone 4. We can add a media max-width 560 and max-height 480 to show only tower cards + wave, hiding powers? But powers are part of gameplay. Alternatively allow dock horizontally scroll? Hmm.

Most modern phones landscape are >=667 width. We support down to 667 well. Good.

Also portrait small (320x568) still works, dock 2 rows and board scaled. Fine.

Need update CSS short landscape overrides. Currently the max-height block is below max-width:800 in source, so overrides work. Add grid properties. Let's edit.

